# fixedbugs, defect 2516, lane b35-link, 2026-11-13.
#
# SYMPTOM: `twice`, which this module's group and another's bind two ways
# and neither module calls: refused with *the linker joins both to one
# symbol* and *C then reaches one `twice` through two types*, false of a
# program whose objects refer to no `twice` (a name bound and never called
# is in no module's table of externs, `emit/extern_refs.hero`).
#
# FIX: the linker is named only where both modules call the name; here the
# note says neither module's C calls it, and the remedy for two bindings
# stands.
use fixedbugs2516/binds_b

extern "fixedbugs-2516-declares-a.h"
    function declares_a_value(x: i64) -> i64
    function twice(x: i64) -> i64  #~ ffi_declared_two_ways

function main()
    print(declares_a_value(x: 3))
    print(binds_b.b(x: 3))
